cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "smp-max: certified maximum numbers of stable matchings (f(5) = 16, f(6) = 48, f(7) >= 85)"
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Jiarui
    email: jxucoder@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/jxucoder/smp-max"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-09
keywords:
  - stable marriage
  - stable matchings
  - Knuth's problem
  - Lean 4
  - SAT certificates
  - cake_lpr
  - OEIS A357269
  - OEIS A357271
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked determination of the maximum number f(n) of stable matchings
  of an n x n stable-marriage instance for n = 5 and n = 6, and a new lower
  bound for n = 7. f(5) = 16 and f(6) = 48 are Lean 4 theorems whose only
  hypothesis is the unsatisfiability of Lean-defined CNF formulas (120 cube
  formulas at order 5; 318,736 cube formulas at order 6), each refuted by a SAT
  solver with the refutation checked by the formally verified LRAT checker
  cake_lpr. f(7) >= 85 is witnessed by two explicit instances.
